CORESIDENT|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=BOOK-04 IV.7 is itself the record of a contradiction the operator caught in one sentence of the seat's prose: 'it never enters the stream, and both sides must hold the same 3,174 bytes.' Held and free cannot both be true; the law resolves it by charging held bytes, and keeps the offending sentence quoted.|tag=CANON|json=0
