CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=MACHINE SPEC: turn [0016] "Twenty gigabytes of GPU, sixteen gigabytes of RAM, and two terabytes of USB hard drive that I use as RAM." against turn [0029] "Oh, that's why my sixty four cores on my computer are running it so fast." Both are his own statements about his own machine and they are not reconciled in this file; the catalogue gloss for [0016] also silently rewrites "USB hard drive" as "sol|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=COST FIGURE: IX.B.5 records "that number of 3 or 2 bc should actually be much more like .15 or less" as a correction to a figure this project had been quoting — but the corrected-from figure ("3 or 2 bc") is nowhere defined in this file, so the correction cannot be checked against what it corrects.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=NAMING: he states "it is the Shannon Laws" (correcting an audio error), then "maybe we should call it the Shannon Brown laws", then asks the trained system to derive the name from his name, then refers to "the RIME 27 laws" — four namings in one day, none actioned, none superseding the others on the record.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-1|text=MACHINE COUNT, four values, never reconciled: "No. Not two machines. Six machines." [0093] → "6 sectors 8 holes= 8 machines" [0094] → "414 machines" [0096] → "the other three machines actually 5 bow" [0145]. Six, eight, 414 and three-actually-five all stand in this slice with no stated relation between them.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-1|text=THREE vs TWENTY-SEVEN, stated one turn apart: "We run the whole world third part" [0129] is immediately overridden by "But it's not gonna be three. It's gonna be twenty seven." [0130], and again at [0149] "we just showed that it works with twenty seven, and I think you are using three." He is correcting the granularity of his own prior sentence, not reversing the principle.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-1|text=PHI vs PIE, explicit self-correction: "the inverted inversion of phi is phi over pi, which is one" [0119] is retracted at [0120] — "No. Not phi over pie. that was the audio. I use the audio when I walk. pie over pie." The earlier form is a transcription artifact of him dictating while walking and is superseded.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-1|text=SMARTER vs BIGGER, inside one turn [0113]: "they grow smarter" and then "They grow the ability to hold more bits." He downgrades his own word in the same breath — the gain is capacity, not intelligence.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-1|text=PRIME DISTANCES: "no one prime to another prime distance is the same" [0197] and "no 1 prime to prime would even state the same distance to another prime to prime" [0239] versus "Oh, the distance is repeat if they're from the same agents." [0240]. He scopes the no-repeat law himself: it holds across different agents, not within one.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-1|text=TEN GIGABYTES, both floor and insult: "You only use ten gigabytes? What? Are you joking me?" [0150] rejects 10 GB as too small, while "you need to start thinking about ten gigabyte scale on everything" [0152] sets 10 GB as the minimum planning scale. Resolved at [0153]: divide the megabytes across many datasets and connect them through the neural net — 10 GB is the floor for the whole, not an acce|tag=CANON|json=0
