CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-2|text=The 1.81 cause is given twice with different causes: [0301] "The reason it doesn't work above one point eight one is because of the clippy issue" against [0301] "It had something to do with the percentage of... it said misplaced antiparticles" — a toolchain lint and a physical-anomaly percentage attributed to the same threshold.|tag=CANON|json=0
CORESIDENT|lane=his-own-voice-2|text="rhyme" vs "rime" is used interchangeably and then explicitly corrected: [0280] "rhyme ejection", [0287] "The rhyme sphere is one container", [0326] "The zero is the rhyme sphere" — against [0284] "Rime jection not a ryhm jection. sorry" and [0281] "not primes, rimes." The corrected spelling does not propagate backwards through the record.|tag=CANON|json=0
